lesson: 98
title: Metres and centimetres
stars: 1
explain: One metre is 100 centimetres. To work with a length in metres and a length in centimetres, first turn the metres into centimetres.
explain: A ribbon 3 metres long is 300 centimetres; cutting off 45 centimetres leaves 300 − 45 = 255 centimetres.
vars: a=name m=2..9 c5=2..19
let: c = c5 * 5
answer: 100 * m - c
exercise: A ribbon is {m} metres long. {a} cuts off {c} centimetres. How many centimetres of ribbon are left?
exercise: {a} has a rope {m} metres long and uses {c} centimetres of it. How many centimetres of rope are left?
exercise: A board is {m} metres long. A piece of {c} centimetres is sawn off. How long is the rest, in centimetres?
exercise: {a} has {m} metres of wire and bends {c} centimetres of it into a ring. How many centimetres of wire are not used?
exercise: A roll of tape is {m} metres long. {a} uses {c} centimetres for a box. How many centimetres of tape remain?
test: Out of a piece of string {m} metres long, {a} cuts {c} centimetres for a kite. What length of string is left over, in centimetres?
test: How many centimetres are left if {c} centimetres are taken from a cloth {m} metres long?
test: {a}'s garden hose was {m} metres long until a {c}-centimetre piece split and was cut away. How long is the hose now, in centimetres?
test: A wall is {m} metres wide. A shelf on it is {c} centimetres shorter than the wall. How many centimetres wide is the shelf?
exercise: {a} cuts {c} centimetres from a ribbon {m} metres long. How many centimetres remain?
exercise: How many centimetres of rope are left if {c} centimetres are cut from a rope of {m} metres?
exercise: {m} metres of string, {c} centimetres used. How many centimetres are left?
exercise: A curtain in a flat in London is {m} metres long. {a} shortens it by {c} centimetres. How long is the curtain now, in centimetres?
exercise: {a} has {m.words} metres of yarn and knits {c} centimetres of it into a scarf. How many centimetres of yarn are left?
exercise: A plank is {m} metres long. {a} saws away {c} centimetres. How many centimetres of plank remain?
exercise: A strip of paper {m} metres long loses {c} centimetres when {a} trims it. What is its length now, in centimetres?
exercise: {a} unrolls {m} metres of fabric and cuts off a {c}-centimetre piece. How many centimetres of fabric are still on the roll?
test: A fence in Melbourne is {m} metres long, but a gate takes up {c} centimetres of it. How many centimetres of the fence are not the gate?
test: In centimetres, what is left of {m} metres of cable after {a} uses {c} centimetres?
test: {a} jumps {c} centimetres short of the {m}-metre mark. How far does {a.he} jump, in centimetres?
test: From a {m}-metre roll of wrapping paper, {c} centimetres are torn off for a gift. How many centimetres of paper are still there?
test: A flag pole in Canada is {m} metres tall. The top of the flag hangs {c} centimetres below the top of the pole. How high above the ground is the top of the flag, in centimetres?
test: Take {c} centimetres away from {m} metres. How many centimetres do you get?
exercise: ribbon {m} m long, cut {c} cm off, how many cm left
exercise: {a} had {m} metres of rope, used {c+5} — no wait, {c} cm. cm left?
exercise: {a} says there's {100*m+c} cm left cos {a.he} added. nah, {m} m rope, {c} cm cut. cm left really
exercise: board {m} metres, sawed off {c} cm, took like 5 minutes lol. how long the rest in cm
test: how many cm left of a {m} metre string if u cut {c} cm
test: {c+10} cm, no sorry, {c} cm cut off a {m} m tape. rest in centimetres?
test: {a} reckons {100*m-c+10} cm left. nah check — {m} metres, {c} cm off. whats left in cm
exam: It is given that a ribbon measures {m} metres in length and that {c} centimetres are severed therefrom. Determine the remaining length in centimetres.
exam: Ascertain, in centimetres, the length of rope remaining in the possession of {a} after {c} centimetres have been utilised from a rope of {m.words} metres.
exam: Whereas a length of cloth of {m} metres is reduced by {c} centimetres, state the residual length, expressed in centimetres.
exam: Compute the difference, in centimetres, between a length of {m} metres and a length of {c} centimetres.
exercise: {a} was "creative with the truth": {a.he} said {a.he} used a tiny bit of the {m}-metre ribbon, but really {a.he} used {c} centimetres. How many centimetres of ribbon are left?
exercise: The cat "made a mess" of the end of a {m}-metre curtain cord, so {c} centimetres had to be cut off. How many centimetres of cord are left?
test: puppy "did its business" on the end of the {m} m rope so i chopped off {c} cm. gross. how many cm left
